Original commit body from ceedfcf:

Replace centrality-only selection with a greedy frontier-based algorithm
that prioritizes nodes bridging disconnected components. This produces
connected subgraphs instead of isolated high-centrality nodes.

Algorithm uses Union-Find for O(α(n)) component tracking with scoring:
(component_growth, edges_added, centrality). Nodes that merge disconnected
entrypoints score highest.

Results (same 200-node budget):
- Django: 21 → 86 edges (4x improvement)
- TensorFlow: 157 → 1775 edges (11x improvement)

Performance: handles tensorflow (154k symbols, 505k edges) in ~6 seconds.

Connectivity-aware is now the default; use --no-connectivity to disable.
